# Server-side/API example only. Replace variables through your authorized HTTP client.
# No credentials are included. POST requires a currently authorized human operator, not M2M.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tickets/{{ticketId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{humanAccessToken}}
X-Workspace-Id: {{workspaceId}}

### Claim self. Use the ETag from GET; never replace the key on an uncertain retry.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tickets/{{ticketId}}/assignments
Authorization: Bearer {{humanAccessToken}}
X-Workspace-Id: {{workspaceId}}
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: {{ticketETag}}
Idempotency-Key: {{stableClaimKey}}

{"action":"claim","reason":"Assumindo a análise técnica da solicitação."}

### Release. Owner or workspace admin, current ETag and a different key for this NEW operation.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tickets/{{ticketId}}/assignments
Authorization: Bearer {{humanAccessToken}}
X-Workspace-Id: {{workspaceId}}
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: {{currentTicketETag}}
Idempotency-Key: {{stableReleaseKey}}

{"action":"release","reason":"Retornando o atendimento à triagem da equipe."}

# 200: successful/no-op/original replay. GET for current state after a replay.
# 403: not operator/scope missing or another owner cannot be released.
# 404: ticket not accessible. Identifiers never authorize.
# 409: occupied, terminal, or idempotency key conflict.
# 412: stale version. Refresh then explicitly review before creating a NEW operation.
# 428: missing If-Match. 503/network error: result may be uncertain; do not blindly re-key.
# No emails/webhooks are sent for responsibility changes in v0.9.0.
